{"id": "en_lost_forest_p1", "total": 66.77, "segments": [{"text": "If you are lost in a deep forest as night falls, do not panic and keep walking.", "start": 0.0, "end": 3.78}, {"text": "Most people make it worse by walking further into the dark instead of stopping.", "start": 4.24, "end": 7.18}, {"text": "Cold snow starts to fall through the trees right now as dusk settles in fast.", "start": 7.78, "end": 10.96}, {"text": "Mark stands still near the trees and uses the S.T.O.P. method to survive.", "start": 11.54, "end": 15.0}, {"text": "One. Stop right now because moving makes searchers miss your last known point completely.", "start": 15.62, "end": 19.38}, {"text": "Two. Think about your next move and observe the freezing environment around you carefully.", "start": 19.94, "end": 23.42}, {"text": "Three. Make yourself visible and audible to anyone who might be searching for you.", "start": 23.88, "end": 27.68}, {"text": "Mark waves his bright jacket in the open space to catch distant rescue eyes.", "start": 27.68, "end": 31.3}, {"text": "He blows 3 sharp whistle blasts because that is the universal distress signal.", "start": 31.68, "end": 34.88}, {"text": "Before dark, you must get out of the wind and off the cold ground.", "start": 35.48, "end": 38.1}, {"text": "Mark puts branches and leaves under his boots to block the freezing soil.", "start": 38.78, "end": 41.4}, {"text": "He builds a small shelter close to a giant tree for extra wind protection.", "start": 41.88, "end": 44.66}, {"text": "He looks past the trees toward a wooden cabin sitting far away in the clearing.", "start": 45.24, "end": 47.98}, {"text": "He knows he should walk to the cabin to sleep in a warm bed tonight.", "start": 48.58, "end": 50.96}, {"text": "Mark stays put near the trees because searchers always start from your last known point.", "start": 51.7, "end": 54.96}, {"text": "It was the perfect survival plan and Mark followed every single official rule.", "start": 55.34, "end": 59.18}, {